, Kinchen SA, Grunbaum JA, Whalen L, Eaton D, Hawkins J, Ross JG: Methodology of the youth risk behavior surveillance system. <source>MMWR Recomm Rep</source> <volume>53</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;13, <year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="r20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Silverstein J, Klingensmith G, Copeland K, Plotnick L, Kaufman F, Laffel L, Deeb L, Grey M, Anderson B, Holzmeister LA, Clark N: Care of children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes: a statement of the American Diabetes Association. <source>Diabetes Care</source> <volume>28</volume>:<fpage>186</fpage>&#x02013;212, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15616254</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="other">U.S Census Bureau: United States Census, 2000. &#x0005b;article online&#x0005d;, <year>2008</year>. Available from <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.census.gov/main/www/cen2000.html">http://www.census.gov/main/www/cen2000.html</ext-link>. Accessed 18 July 2008</citation></ref><ref id="r22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Howe CJ, Jawad AF, Kelly SD, Lipman TH: Weight-related concerns and behaviors in children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes. <source>J Am Psychiatr Nurses Assoc</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>376</fpage>&#x02013;385, <year>2008</year></citation></ref><ref id="r23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Jones JM, Lawson ML, Daneman D, Olmsted MP, Rodin G: Eating disorders in adolescent females with and without type 1 diabetes: cross sectional study. <source>BMJ</source> <volume>320</volume>:<fpage>1563</fpage>&#x02013;1566, <year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10845962</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ogden CL, Carroll MD, Flegal KM: High body mass index for age among US children and adolescents, 2003&#x02013;2006. <source>JAMA</source> <volume>299</volume>:<fpage>2401</fpage>&#x0