>Data are means &#x000b1; SD or <italic>n</italic> (&#x00025;).</p></fn><fn id="t1fn1"><label>&#x0002a;</label><p><italic>P</italic> values derived from &#x003c7;<sup>2</sup> tests for categorical variables and <italic>t</italic> test for continuous variables, showing associations with diabetes type (type 1 versus type 2 diabetes) stratified by sex.</p></fn><fn id="t1fn2"><label>&#x02020;</label><p><italic>P</italic> values derived from &#x003c7;<sup>2</sup> tests for categorical variables and <italic>t</italic> test for continuous variables, showing associations with sex (type 1 and type 2 diabetes combined).</p></fn><fn id="t1fn3"><label>&#x02021;</label><p>Among youth who reported ever trying to lose weight.</p></fn><fn id="t1fn4"><label>&#x000a7;</label><p>Among those who reported ever trying to lose weight and were taking insulin at the time of the study visit. GED, general equivalency degree (high school).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="t2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Associations between each healthy and unhealthy weight-loss practices and diabetes type, by sex, among 1,646 youth aged &#x02265;10 years of age who had ever tried to lose weight</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="2" align="center" valign="bottom"/><th colspan="2" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Healthy weight-loss practices<hr/></th><th colspan="4" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Unhealthy weight-loss practices<hr/></th></tr><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Exercise</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Diet</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Fasting</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Diet aids</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Vomiting/laxatives</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Skip insulin</th></tr></thead><t